    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that, but it feels like the \"valid concerns\" often get used as excuses to keep housing prices sky high. like, if every neighborhood just blocks density because they're worried about \"character,\" isn't that basically just a way to keep people out? wouldn't you say that these arguments are ultimately just a barrier to economic growth and housing equity?",
